  ($q$Kenyan Wildlife & Culture$q$, $q$The sacred Kaya forests, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, belong to which coastal people?$q$, $q$The Mijikenda$q$, $q$The Maasai$q$, $q$The Luo$q$, $q$The Turkana$q$, 'a', 'hard', $q$The Kayas are old forest villages that the Mijikenda still treat as sacred.$q$),
  ($q$Kenyan Wildlife & Culture$q$, $q$Thimlich Ohinga, a stone-walled UNESCO World Heritage Site, is in which county?$q$, $q$Kisumu$q$, $q$Migori$q$, $q$Nandi$q$, $q$Narok$q$, 'b', 'hard', $q$It was listed in 2018 and is several centuries old.$q$),
